{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced avgpool with transformer aggregation in the multiprofile scvi_n200 RNA-only setting (the single-variable change from the current best, config_005), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.653 and F1 of 0.628 versus 0.650 and 0.628 for avgpool. The negligible ~0.3-point accuracy difference suggests that a more expressive transformer aggregation provides no meaningful improvement over simple average pooling for combining multi-profile scvi_n200 representations, indicating the aggregation axis is near its practical ceiling under the current encoder. It remains uncertain whether this null result generalizes to other encoders (e.g., scgpt) or whether the remaining headroom lies in the encoder-choice axis or the multimodal fusion question, which are the next unexplored design axes."
}

